To find the difference $f(x) - g(x)$, we subtract the corresponding terms:

\begin{align*}
f(x) - g(x) &= (x^2 + 3x + 2) - (2x + 1) \\
&= x^2 + 3x + 2 - 2x - 1 \\
&= x^2 + x + 1.
\end{align*}

So, the difference $f(x) - g(x)$ is $x^2 + x + 1$.

